# GitHub workflow

- Work is a GitHub issue on the Ceraghit project (#19). Labels: `priority: high|medium|low` plus an area label.
- Start with `pnpm start-issue <n>` (or `gh issue develop <n> --checkout`): branch and PR auto-link to the issue.
- One issue per PR, PR title short and plain, body says what and why plus `Closes #n`. PR template has a preview check.
- Every PR gets a Dokploy preview and a sticky "Preview deployments" comment (`scripts/deploy/dokploy.mjs`), plus a
  GitHub deployment. Test the change on that link. It is deleted when the PR closes.
- CI (`ci.yml`): `lint` (+ rules sync + migration drift), `types`, `test` with Postgres, `build`, `e2e` (Playwright,
  uploads `e2e-artifacts`) and `audit` (advisories, licenses). Separate workflows: `pr-body.yml` (`Closes #n` + inline
  screenshots) and `migrations.yml` (additive only, one open migration PR). CI uses the Turborepo remote cache on the-keep.
- PR body follows `.github/pull_request_template.md` with screenshots from `pnpm pr:screenshots`. Merge conditions and
  the squash command are in `docs/pr-process.md`.
- Production deploys on merge to `main` (`deploy.yml`): migrate Neon, deploy three Vercel projects, smoke test `/health`.
  Vercel builds only `main` (`deploymentEnabled` in each app's `vercel.json`); PRs use the Dokploy preview.
- Agents never commit, push, or post review replies unless the owner authorises it in his own message; otherwise they
  show a diff summary and a suggested message.
